# Optional convenience for development.
#
# Omakei normally learns its folder when you attach one in the editor, and
# remembers it in $XDG_STATE_HOME/omakei/state.json (by default
# ~/.local/state/omakei/state.json).
#
# OMAKEI_STATEMENTS_DIR *seeds* that state on first run. It does not override
# it: once a folder has been attached, the saved one wins and this variable is
# ignored. Setting it alone therefore does nothing on a machine you have
# already used Omakei on.
#
# To develop without touching your real statements, move the state file too, so
# there is no saved folder for the seed to lose to:
#
#   npm run dev:isolated
#
# which is exactly:
#
#   XDG_STATE_HOME="$PWD/.dev/state" \
#   OMAKEI_STATEMENTS_DIR="$PWD/.dev/statements" npm run dev
#
# Both paths are gitignored. Your real state.json is neither read nor written.
#
# NOTE: these must be exported in your environment, not read from this file.
# Vite does not load .env files into process.env, and the ledger API plugin
# never calls loadEnv, so a value set only here never reaches the server.
#
# Never put real statements in the git repo.
